THE ATTACK BEING REPRODUCED
---------------------------
E2eSasGate registers the receiver that carries ACTION_E2E_SAS_RESULT. If that
receiver is EXPORTED, any other app on the device can broadcast

    am broadcast -a com.dnkdialer.companion.E2E_SAS_RESULT \
                 -p com.dnkdialer.companion \
                 --es pairingId <id> --ez sasMatched true

and APPROVE THE SAS on the user's behalf — the whole man-in-the-middle defence
defeated without the digits ever being compared. On minSdk 26 / API 26-32 a
bare registerReceiver(receiver, filter) for an implicit action is exactly that.

The broadcast above is issued through UiAutomation.executeShellCommand, so its
sender is the SHELL user (uid 2000): a genuinely external sender holding
neither our package identity nor the signature permission
com.dnkdialer.companion.DYNAMIC_RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED_PERMISSION.

