  XML: e2e/vc67/evidence/sas-spoof-negative-api34-GREEN.xml

  Both cells require the gate to reach TIMED_OUT after the uid-2000 broadcast:
  the intent is not delivered at all, so the gate can only hit its deadline.

  The first cell carries the POSITIVE CONTROL. Before spoofing, it sends the
  IDENTICAL intent IN-PROCESS and requires the gate to close with MATCHED. A
  green built on absence alone would also be produced by a mistyped action, a
  wrong extra name, or a gate that never armed; the control is what makes the
  negative evidence about the export flag rather than about the intent.

