COVERAGE NOTE — WHAT THIS RUN DOES NOT COVER
--------------------------------------------
API 34 exercises the PLATFORM RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED flag. It does NOT exercise
the API 26-32 path, which is the one F-3 is actually about and which no AVD in
this lane runs. Below API 33 ContextCompat registers the receiver under the
signature-level permission androidx.core declares in its manifest
(<applicationId>.DYNAMIC_RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED_PERMISSION, protectionLevel
signature) — verified by reading core-1.12.0.aar's AndroidManifest.xml in this
lane, not assumed. That path is covered by the SOURCE pin
E2eReceiverExportContractTest, which asserts every registration in
app/src/main goes through ContextCompat and therefore cannot be exported on
ANY API level, plus the lint rule now failing the build on a bare call.

An API-26 on-device run of this same class would close that last gap and the
AVD exists (e2e_api26). It is not part of this lane: booting a second image
breaks the one-emulator-at-a-time rule this run was held to, and the two
checks above already make an exported registration unshippable.

